  "goodToKnow": "Der Leichnam is a formal, respectful word for a dead body; the everyday word is die Leiche: Nur über meine Leiche! (over my dead body!). Fronleichnam (Corpus Christi, from the old word fron, of the Lord) is a Catholic public holiday in several southern and western German states, celebrated with processions in June. Plural: die Leichname."
